<Frame
  title="About — Ben Stannard"
  description="Steel, Coal and the inevitable heat death of the universe"
  indexLabel="PROFILE"
>
  <h1 class="page-label">Steel, Coal and the inevitable heat death of the universe</h1>

  <div class="about">
    <div class="about__portrait">
      <Photo
        src={null}
        alt="Ben Stannard"
        ratio="3 / 4"
        loading="eager"
        placeholderLabel="Portrait"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="about__text">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Obsessed with the magic of film, I've been using it to bottle the grit of European industry for years. It allows me a form of escape from the confusion of modern life. The world is so far removed from the grit of the machines that enable its existence. Witness their terror through the medium format and embrace the void between the now and the then. I've been stuck there, and escapism has always been imperative. Through mostly 120mm film I open a new world into the unknown, embrace the void and let the film's emulsion do the rest. Watch Europe's industrial legacy disintegrate in spectacular colours and allow the machine to come alive.

Feel free to reach out I'm always up for a chat.
      
      </div>

      <dl class="details label">
        {
          details.map((detail) => (
            <div class="details__row">
              <dt>{detail.term}</dt>
              <dd>{detail.value}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</Frame>

<style>
